# Directories under */tests/ that ci.yml's "EXIT-trap safety net" loop does NOT
# point tools/check-harness-net.sh at — one per line, each with its reason.
#
# THIS IS A LIST OF NAMED UNKNOWNS, NOT A PASS LIST. Until 2026-08-30 the loop
# enumerated `git ls-files '*/tests/lib.sh'`, so a suite with no shared net was
# not a failing row — it was not a row (TODO 15.1). Four directories were
# invisible to CI for as long as the step had existed. Three were enrolled the
# same day; what is left is written down here, where it can be read, rather than
# left implicit in an enumeration.
#
# The loop refuses a stale entry two ways, by name: one naming a directory that
# no longer exists, and one naming a directory that has since gained a lib.sh
# and could therefore be checked.

# The meta-checkers' own tests. check-harness-net.sh's first section asks for a
# shared tests/lib.sh, and these deliberately have none: several of them test
# lib.sh-shaped things, and a checker that sourced the harness it is checking
# would be supplying its own subject — the same argument check-harness-net.sh
# makes for providing its own verdict helpers.
#
# IT DOES HAVE A run-all.sh (since 2026-08-30, TODO 15.8), and that is not the
# same question. A runner buckets exit codes; the net is a shared harness the
# tests would have to source. This exemption is about the second only, which is
# why the loop's staleness check asks whether a lib.sh has appeared here — not
# whether anything else has.
tools/tests
